stion/id #uuid "f53c4ccd-94af-5246-9570-8833f9bda16f" :question/math-academy-id "q-317654" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$ \n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{6}⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,5,-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317654/field-1" "q-317654/field-2" "q-317654/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
